AB  - The rapid adoption of Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines has revolutionized software delivery, with platforms like GitHub Actions processing over 100 million workflow runs daily. However, this velocity introduces significant security surfaces. In addition, 87% of organizations report experiencing CI/CD-related security incidents. Existing solutions predominantly rely on static analysis (SAST) or Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) scanning, leaving a critical blind spot: runtime execution vulnerabilities. To address this, we present SafeOps-LogMiner, a real-time security monitoring framework that extends the SafeOps+ platform. Our system introduces a novel hierarchical two-phase machine learning pipeline designed for noise robustness. Phase 1 utilizes a binary logistic regression model with intentional label noise injection (2%) to distinguish benign from vulnerable logs with 97.40% accuracy. Phase 2 deploys a multi-class classifier trained with 3% feature perturbation to identify specific attack vectors (e.g., SQL Injection, Secret Leaks) with 97.00% accuracy. Implemented as a scalable 5-microservice architecture orchestrated via Docker Compose and RabbitMQ, the system processes 10,000+ webhooks per hour with an end-to-end latency of 340 ms. Furthermore, we integrate Generative AI (Google Gemini API) to provide automated remediation patches with 94% syntactic correctness.
ER  - 

