AB  - Particularly software project management has seen fast and amazing development in recent years since the world has grown in need of sophisticated and large-scale software to easily and quickly meet our needs for daily life transactions. Nonetheless, several persistent issues continue to occur in the software sector despite the fierce and quick competition; one such issue is delay in client software delivery resulting from inadequate management policies. Conventional management techniques fall short in reaching the required efficiency and productivity in procedures of decision-making. To maintain competitiveness and productivity with better efficiency, some companies are looking for management methods and tools that help them achieve their goals with tools that reduce the percentage of errors, time, and effort. Artificial intelligence tools were among the most important advanced tools that contributed to keeping pace with this development, and because of the advanced and rapid features that these tools contain, managers resorted to using them to help them reduce the administrative burden during the project.
